{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And there shall be a great cry.</b> Nowhere else in all of Scripture do we find it said \"like it there has never been,\" and \"like it there shall never again be,\" with the word על missing. And so it is: אשר כמוהו לא נהיתה, and על כמוהו לא תוסיף צעקה:" "And the meaning of \"like it\": destruction, or breaking, or death, and what resembles them:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The text appears to be explaining a grammatical anomaly in the verse: the preposition על is absent before כמוהו לא תוסיף, contrary to its presence before כמוהו לא נהיתה. The passage is textually difficult and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:21.642852418Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}